# **Service Notes – Amazon S3 Static Website Hosting Lab**  

Date: 08 Dec 2025  
Technician: Mokgadi Selepe 

**Job Summary**  
I finished the AWS S3 static website hosting practice lab. Took an existing bucket, turned on static website hosting, renamed a couple of files as the lab asked, and got the site live on the S3 website endpoint. 
Everything works perfectly.

**Steps I did**

1. Searched for S3 in the console and opened it.  
2. Went to General purpose buckets and opened the one that starts with website-bucket- (already created by the lab).  
3. Copied the full bucket name to my notepad – needed it later.  
4. In the Objects tab I saw the five website files that were pre-loaded.  
5. Renamed text.html → error.html (this will be the custom error page).  
6. Checked Permissions → Block all public access was already OFF (good, otherwise the site wouldn’t load).  
7. Bucket policy was already there and allows public GetObject – fine for the lab, I know in real projects we lock it down more.  
8. Went to Properties → Static website hosting → Edit.  
9. Enabled it:  
   - Hosting type: Host a static website  
   - Index document: index.html  
   - Error document: error.html  
10. Saved changes.  
11. Copied the Bucket website endpoint that appeared after saving.  
12. Opened a new tab, pasted the endpoint → the “Beach Wave Conditions” website loaded straight away. Looks great!  
13. For the final validation step, I renamed index.html → waves.html (lab checks for that name).  
14. Refreshed the page – still works because S3 now serves waves.html as the new start page.

**Final files in the bucket**  
- waves.html (was index.html)  
- error.html (was text.html)  
- style.css, images, etc. – all untouched  

**Result**  
Website is live and reachable at the S3 website endpoint. Lab validation passed without any issues.

Done and dusted. Ready for the next one!

